      "content": "That makes sense. I want to get a bit deeper into the \"intelligence\" aspect for the module, because managers often use \"communication skills\" as a polite way to mask more direct judgments. \n\nIf we were to look at it from a more \"realistic\" or \"data-driven\" perspective that some managers claim to use, how do these linguistic differences actually correlate with things like cognitive ability or leadership potential in high-pressure corporate environments? I'm trying to understand if there's a way to frame this for managers who argue that \"standard English\" is simply a more efficient or logical way to communicate complex ideas.",
